==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*1 [[Wicked Face]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*3 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 56.67~60 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 70~76.67 seconds<sup>2,100f~2,300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Bring high-range attackers like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] to counter the Condemned Pengs, as well as a Shield Piercer to make getting rid of Wicked Face a whole lot easier. High damage nukers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] help during periods of downtime as well and against Aku Gory.

It is helpful to bring [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to block Wicked Face's Waves, but do note that he is likely to die easily to the buffed peons due to his plus levels being nullified and his base levels being capped. Because of this, generic and spamable/tanky [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immune]] units such as [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] or [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] are recommended to stall if you've raised the level cap on said units.

